 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(W \cdot H)$ to generate origins and directions, where $W$ and $H$ are image width and height.
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(W \cdot H)$ to store the origins and directions arrays.
-- **Strengths:** No perspective distortion; parallel lines remain parallel; uniform sampling density across the image plane regardless of depth.
-- **Limitations:** No depth cueing via size reduction; not suitable for scenes requiring realistic depth perception.
-- **When to use:** Technical visualization, CAD, scientific data visualization where accurate spatial relationships are critical.
-- **When not to use:** Realistic rendering requiring depth cues, scenes with large depth ranges where perspective is needed for clarity.
