 ## Background
-Orthographic projection is a fundamental concept in computer graphics, used to flatten the 3D scene onto a two-dimensional plane without perspective distortion [S3, unofficial]. It is commonly used in technical drawing and visualization tools such as Smokeview for fire dynamics simulation data [S3, unofficial]. The method is implemented in OpenGL via `glOrtho` [S3, unofficial]. In modern differentiable rendering, orthographic cameras are used in methods like VoGE for point cloud rendering [S2, unofficial].
